{"event": {"id": "b7fd1f20b4fe", "type": "feature.pre_implement", "at": "2026-10-19T11:18:45Z", "payload": {"feature": "harness-hygiene", "text": "Harness hygiene (H1-H8)\nFix audit findings H1-H8 before optimizing.\nunittest discover passes without pytest installed\nSuite runs from repo root without manual pythonpath\ndiscovery/gates detect Python stack and a test gate in this repo\nOwner inference matches whole words, not substrings\nTasks without explicit depends_on are not chained serially by default\nmetrics record-round --append writes the row atomically\n- [ ] T001 Record baseline counts (unittest: 502 run / 21 errors; pytest with flag: 631; pytest from root: 62 collection errors; `gates detect --path .`: no test gate) in specs/013-harness-hygiene/validation-report.md\n- [ ] T002 [US1] Write AST-guided converter in the session scratchpad (not shipped) that wraps module-level `test_*` functions into a `unittest.TestCase`, turns `@pytest.fixture` into `_fixture_<name>` helpers and `tmp_path` into a per-test temp dir; bodies/asserts kept verbatim\n- [ ] T003 [P] [US1] Convert graph modules spec-master/tests/test_graph_{blast_radius,context,drift,enrichment,health,maps,model,ontology,parser,query,resolver,store,temporal,traversal,validation}.py\n- [ ] T004 [P] [US1] Convert knowledge modules spec-master/tests/test_knowledge_{manifest,model,profiles,router,validation}.py and spec-master/tests/test_traceability_graph.py\n- [ ] T005 [P] [US1] Wrap unittest-invisible modules spec-master/tests/test_{context_budget,evals,runtime_contract,tool_policy}.py\n- [ ] T006 [US1] Verify per-module test names before/after are identical (scratchpad script) and that no module in spec-master/tests imports pytest; run unittest discover (expect ≥ 631, OK)\n- [ ] T007 [US2] Reproduce failure: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest spec-master/tests -q` → `No module named '_pathfix'` (RED)\n- [ ] T008 [US2] Add path-only spec-master/tests/conftest.py (no pytest import) inserting its directory into sys.path; re-run root pytest with and without path (GREEN)\n- [ ] T009 [P] [US3] Add failing tests to spec-master/tests/test_discovery.py: unittest suite in `<child>/tests` detected with `python3 -m unittest discover -s <child>/tests`; pytest-importing suite → `python3 -m pytest <dir>`; root `tests/` detected; hidden/`node_modules`/`.venv` suites ignored; dir without test files ignored; manifest repo unchanged (no `scope` key, command `pytest`)\n- [ ] T010 [P] [US3] Add failing tests to spec-master/tests/test_quality_gates.py: suite stack yields blocking gate named `test (python: <scope>)`; two suites yield two distinct gate names\n- [ ] T011 [US3] Implement `_scan_python_test_suites()` and the no-manifest fallback in spec-master/lib/discovery.py\n- [ ] T012 [US3] Implement scope-aware gate naming in spec-master/lib/quality_gates.py; run `gates detect --path .` on this repo and preflight the returned command\n- [ ] T013 [US4] Add failing tests to spec-master/tests/test_team_model.py: \"Build CLI parser\" not frontend-dev, \"Compute capital gains report\" not backend-dev, \"Collect feedback\" / \"Write user guide\" fall back to fullstack-dev, plurals (\"Render dashboard screens\", \"Expose REST endpoints\") still match, path tokens (\"spec-master/lib/ui.py\") match; string tasks and dict tasks without `depends_on` get `[]`; explicit `depends_on` preserved\n- [ ] T014 [US4] Implement token-based `_infer_owner` and remove implicit chaining in spec-master/lib/team_model.py\n- [ ] T015 [P] [US5] Add failing tests to spec-master/tests/test_metrics.py: `append_round` creates missing file (and parent dir), appends in order, refuses invalid JSON / non-list leaving file untouched, leaves no temp files; CLI `--append` twice → two rows; CLI without `--append` writes nothing; CLI on corrupt file exits 1\n- [ ] T016 [US5] Implement `metrics.append_round()` in spec-master/lib/metrics.py and `--append` in spec-master/lib/cli.py\n- [ ] T017 Update spec-master/PROTOCOL.md (Step 6 metrics append + workstreams no implicit chaining, Step 7 suite-detected gates) and README.md where they document the changed behaviour\n- [ ] T018 Record H6 → feature 17 and H7 → feature 14 deferral in specs/013-harness-hygiene/validation-report.md\n- [ ] T019 Run quality gates (unittest, pytest, gates detect + preflight, evals run, graph validate), confirm no third-party import in spec-master/lib or spec-master/tests (FR-013), and write specs/013-harness-hygiene/validation-report.md; add traceability rows", "paths": ["spec-master/tests/test_traceability_graph.py", "spec-master/tests/conftest.py", "spec-master/tests/test_discovery.py", "tests/", "hidden/", "spec-master/tests/test_quality_gates.py", "spec-master/lib/discovery.py", "spec-master/lib/quality_gates.py", "spec-master/tests/test_team_model.py", "spec-master/lib/ui.py", "spec-master/lib/team_model.py", "spec-master/tests/test_metrics.py", "spec-master/lib/metrics.py", "spec-master/lib/cli.py", "spec-master/PROTOCOL.md", "README.md"]}}, "fired": [{"hook": "sensitivity-public-contract", "action": "raise_tier", "directive": {"hook": "sensitivity-public-contract", "type": "raise_tier", "category": "public_contract", "floor": "M", "feature": "harness-hygiene"}}, {"hook": "sensitivity-external-provider", "action": "raise_tier", "directive": {"hook": "sensitivity-external-provider", "type": "raise_tier", "category": "external_provider", "floor": "M", "feature": "harness-hygiene"}}]}
